# PHPDoc Standards

## Language

Documentation is Brazilian Portuguese, matching the entity and facade blocks.

## Class block

Every entity class and `Bling` includes:

- One sentence naming the resource (`Entidade para interação com contatos.`).
- `@see` pointing at the Bling reference section for that resource.

Copy the header in `src/Entities/CamposCustomizados/CamposCustomizados.php` or `src/Entities/Nfes/Nfes.php`. `Bling` documents each getter with `@property`.

## Method block

Each public entity method documents, in this order:

1. **Description** — one Portuguese sentence.
2. **`@param`** — `{type} $name` and a short Portuguese description, one tag per parameter.
3. **`@return`** — the PHP type. Use `null` when `fromResponse` returns `null`.
4. **`@throws BlingApiException|BlingInternalException`** — on every method that calls `$this->repository`.
5. **`@see`** — the Bling operation URL.

Omit `@param` when the method takes no arguments. `Homologacao::execute` returns `void`, calls other entity methods, and documents `@return void` plus `@see https://developer.bling.com.br/homologacao`.

## Schema and enum blocks

- A `*Params` or `*Response` class has a one-line Portuguese summary (`Parâmetros da busca de contatos paginados.`).
- Constructor `@param` tags list every argument with the same type the signature uses, including `Enum|scalar|null` and `\DateTimeInterface|string|null`.
- An enum file starts with `Enumerador de ...`.
- `fromResponse` and `fromRules` use `@inheritDoc` when they implement the base contract.

## Repository, contracts, and exceptions

- Repository methods that implement `IBlingRepository` use `@inheritDoc` (`BlingRepository`).
- The interface method documents `@param RequestOptions $options` and `@return ResponseOptions`.
- Exception classes document the purpose in Portuguese and list constructor parameters in signature order.

## Links

Base reference: `https://developer.bling.com.br/referencia`.

Use the URL-encoded resource name already present on sibling methods (`Contatos`, `Campos%20Customizados`, `Border%C3%B4s`). The operation anchor uses the Bling pattern `get_contatos__idContato_`.
